      "title": "Codex sandbox mode is inherited from the machine config despite the documented override promise",
      "issue_number": 365,
      "body": "Found by WP-F5 (#102 launch diagnosis) and classified by its independent GPT-6.1 Sol review on 2026-10-19 as a documentation and contract defect. Outside every I01 to I07 bolt; filed for triage.\n\n## Defect\n\ndocs/06 (line 83 at `9070207`) and the comment at `packages/adapter-codex/src/options.ts:5` promise that GraphGoblin overrides every behaviour-affecting Codex default so nothing from the machine's `config.toml` leaks into loops. The machine's `[windows] sandbox = \"elevated\"` setting does reach the Codex sessions GraphGoblin starts through the SDK (observed in the WP-F5 trial session logs and reproduced with `codex sandbox`).\n\n## Expected\n\nEither the promise holds (the backend selection is set explicitly per session) or the documentation and the comment name the settings that are inherited and why.\n\n## Actual\n\nBackend sandbox mode is inherited from the user's configuration. Inheriting it does not itself weaken the authored sandbox permissions, so this is a contract and documentation gap rather than a confirmed permission defect.\n\n## Fix shape\n\nNarrow the promise in docs/06 and `options.ts`, or define the backend explicitly in the session options and test that the machine setting is ignored.\n\n## Related\n\n#102 (record `docs/qa/2026-10-19-wp-f5-launch-diagnosis.md`), docs/06 \"Windows notes\".\n",
